    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1071">

                <pb facs="0953" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg849"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/9361.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Great Britain to the
                        Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-24T20:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 24, 1913—8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. Department’s October 24, 6 p.m. Would you favor authorizing me to ascertain
                    whether the British Government as an act of friendliness <pb facs="0954" n="850"
                        xml:id="pg850"/> will refrain from recognizing anyone claiming to be elected
                    President of Mexico at the elections of October 26 until our Government has had
                    reasonable time to consider its course?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
